{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And I am grown old.</b> From here the Sages said (Bava Metzi'a, chapter השוכר) that one is permitted to modify for the sake of peace — for she said, 'And my master is old,' and the Holy One, blessed be He, modified and said, 'And I am grown old.' And even though according to the plain reading it seems that she too said 'And I am grown old,' for it is written אחרי בלותי — one may say: it could be that for me there is a remedy to bear children, for 'אחרי בלותי היתה לי עדנה' — for I have had menstrual discharge, but for my husband there is no remedy, for 'ואדוני זקן.' And so it seems to me, that the language implies 'היתה לי' — and will not be. And there are those who say: Heaven forbid that the Place would modify, for 'דובר שקרים לא יכון לנגד עיניו' — and she too said 'And I am grown old,' and the meaning of 'אחרי בלותי' etc. is in wonderment, and He modified for the sake of peace in that He did not recount all her words but only some of them. And all other people are permitted to modify entirely. And if you ask: what indignation would Abraham have if she said that he is old? — one may say: it means that he grinds but does not emit."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The citation '(מציע' פ' השוכר)' refers to Bava Metzi'a; the tractate name is abbreviated as מציעה and I have rendered it accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:36.191655466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}